## 5. Guardrails

- `offset` belongs in the data layer (`LIMIT … OFFSET …`) or applied to the full ordered set — never to an already-truncated page.
- Validate `offset` on ingress (`non-negative integer`, `400 VALIDATION_ERROR`) like `limit`.
- Keep `total` independent of `limit`/`offset`.
- `hasMore` probe (`limit+1`) and the offset window are orthogonal: fetch `[offset, offset+limit+1)` and drop the extra after the probe.
- Ranked/embedding paths page over a bounded score-ordered pool and degrade to empty beyond it, never to unordered rows.
